-    - Flood-fill 4-connectedly from the blue indicator, treating the grey wall as blocked; the reached cells are the inner region and the remaining non-wall cells are the outer region.
-    - In each region, each same-color pair defines one periodic ray: its shared row/column is the ray axis, and the pair's distance along that axis is the period.
-    - Start from the pair point that is closer to the relevant grid edge, then march away from that edge in period-sized jumps until leaving the grid.
-    - Paint only the jump positions that belong to the same region as that pair; positions on the wall or in the other region are skipped while later jumps are still checked.
